    "long_instructions": "Sasha’s finally ready to open her salon in Regreston. Regreston has a population of 5,000 and one existing salon. Sasha will keep her salon open on weekends, and it will offer full-service.\r\n\r\nHow many customers does your model predict Sasha will have every month?\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember you can get a prediction with `model.predict`, then print that prediction.\r\n\r\n```\r\nprediction = model.predict(...)\r\nprint(prediction)\r\n```\r\n\r\nConsider the argument you’ll pass to `model.predict` to match Bob’s description. It must be a list of encoded feature values inside a list itself. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\nprediction = model.predict([[5, 1, 1, 0, 1, 0]])\r\n```\r\n\r\nOrder your feature value in the same order as the columns of your feature matrix. Remember that `OneHotEncoder` creates columns alphabetically.",
